  "description": "Retrospective application for a pergola in the rear garden",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-42605106-7fff-4a73-4c3d-a298797c65ed&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The pergola, by reason of its inappropriate scale, form, detailed design and materials, would result in an incongruous, visually intrusive and unsympathetic feature that adversely detracts from&amp;nbsp; the setting of the Grade II Listed buildings and fails to preserve the character and appearance of the Clapton Square Conservation Area. No public benefits have been identified to outweigh this harm. For these reasons, the development is contrary to Policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033, Policies D3 (Optimising Site Capacity through the Design Led Approach), HC1 (Heritage Conservation and Growth) of the London Plan, and paragraph 206 of the NPPF.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
